{
  "id": "ep078",
  "duration": 59.131,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.587,
      "text": "Our universe could vanish in an instant with zero warning.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustration of an Isolated Black Hole (52675793824).png",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_an_Isolated_Black_Hole_(52675793824).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.587,
      "end": 11.907,
      "text": "This terrifying possibility stems from false vacuum decay, a metastable state where local stability could suddenly collapse.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustration of an Isolated Black Hole (52675793824).png",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_an_Isolated_Black_Hole_(52675793824).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 11.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.907,
      "end": 19.227,
      "text": "The theoretical framework for this catastrophic process was established by Sidney Coleman in 1977.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.9,
          "end": 19.233,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.227,
      "end": 25.622,
      "text": "Standard Model calculations place the electroweak vacuum in this fragile, metastable region.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "CERN Collider, France-Switzerland (ASTER).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/METI/AIST/Japan Space Systems, and U.S./Japan ASTER Science Team",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CERN_Collider,_France-Switzerland_(ASTER).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.233,
          "end": 25.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.622,
      "end": 34.322,
      "text": "Calculations of the Standard Model vacuum lifetime estimate it exceeds 10 to the 65 to 10 to the 100 years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.633,
          "end": 34.333,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.322,
      "end": 44.067,
      "text": "Yet researchers recently simulated these universe-destroying bubbles using a 5,564-qubit quantum annealer from D-Wave.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "DWave 128chip.jpg",
        "credit": "D-Wave Systems, Inc.",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DWave_128chip.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.333,
          "end": 44.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.067,
      "end": 51.937,
      "text": "Published in Nature Physics in 2025, these findings prove a bubble of true vacuum could expand at the speed of light.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Hole punch clouds over the Bahamas (16109909541).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center from Greenbelt, MD, USA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hole_punch_clouds_over_the_Bahamas_(16109909541).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.067,
          "end": 48.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 51.937,
      "end": 58.781,
      "text": "Because a bubble of true vacuum could expand at light speed, our universe could vanish in an instant with zero warning.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustration of an Isolated Black Hole (52675793824).png",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_an_Isolated_Black_Hole_(52675793824).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 51.933,
          "end": 59.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
